3. AUTHENTICATION METHODS

Implement two supported authentication methods.

A. Google Sign-In

Use secure Google OAuth/OIDC authentication through the appropriate supported authentication service.

The application must:

- Open the official Google sign-in flow.
- Never request or store the user's Google password.
- Receive a verified identity token/session from the authentication provider.
- Create or locate the corresponding application account.
- Sign the user into the app.
- Load their authorised school data.

Store a stable authentication/provider identifier rather than relying only on the user's display name.

